# WEATHERONLINE (RC_JOBS=rc.jobs.weatheronline): give Weather a link, then
# let it ask.  The weatherlog canary (logs/151121-run.log) finally put the
# library inside Weather itself and showed what its WeatherKit client does:
# a PUT to weather-edge.apple.com/v1/configs and a GET to c.apple.news, both
# through URLSession and both answered "The Internet connection appears to be
# offline" -- the boot had no Wi-Fi.  The forecast request (the one a data
# shim has to answer) never came because the client stopped at its config
# fetch.  This run joins the network written in fw/network first, so those
# requests can succeed and the next one can be seen: its host, its path and
# whether it carries an Authorization header.
/redwood/bin/net_test wait 20 joinfile /redwood/fw/network
/redwood/bin/weatherprefs
/redwood/bin/sleep_hold 420 &
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 30
/var/jb/usr/bin/uiopen --bundleid com.apple.weather
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 20
/redwood/bin/rwtouch tap 0.5 0.699
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 10
/redwood/bin/rwtouch tap 0.5 0.699
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 120
